fory provides CMake targets. Link against Fory::fory to pull in the full
Apache Fory C++ serialization and row-format libraries:

    find_package(Fory CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(my_target PRIVATE Fory::fory)

Fine-grained component targets are also available: Fory::serialization
(binary serialization only) and Fory::row_format (row format + encoder).

Target alias contract: the upstream Fory CMake install exports targets in
the fory:: namespace (e.g. fory::fory_lib). This overlay port injects
capitalised-namespace aliases (Fory::fory, Fory::serialization,
Fory::row_format) via ForyAliases.cmake, which is automatically included by
ForyConfig.cmake. Consumers MUST use Fory::fory, not fory::fory_lib, to
remain insulated from upstream namespace changes. The alias file also
declares find_dependency(absl) so that a missing Abseil installation
produces a clear CMake error at configure time rather than a cryptic linker
error at build time.

This is a glibre overlay port. The canonical upstream port in
microsoft/vcpkg should be preferred once it ships.
